        ":question/id": "5fad567a-778a-50da-9a67-5a6c9f8617a0",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int -8{sec}^{2}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int {sec}^{2}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z=tan⁡z+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int -8{sec}^{2}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z & =-8\\int {sec}^{2}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =-8(tan⁡z)+C \\\\  & =-8tan⁡z+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
