        ":question/id": "d57ebf80-c4f4-5872-a02e-c71994c830ec",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int sec⁡x(4sec⁡x+7tan⁡x)\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =sec⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =tan⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int sec⁡x(4sec⁡x+7tan⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{sec}^{2}⁡x+7sec⁡xtan⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 4{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 7sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4tan⁡x+7sec⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      "role": "independently authored inventory",
      "relationship_to_source_templates": "Same distributed secant family and complete bank as q-49122, with changed coefficients."
